[0.001, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[97mThe hard family tell\u001b[93m C:\\builder_v2\\stealc\\json.h\u001b[97m is present (file offset 0x7e756, UTF-16). WinMain was already renamed\r\n\u001b[93mstealc_main_cis_locale_and_single_instance_gate\u001b[97m. Let me decompile it.\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                      \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Callisto) · ▸ get_function(stealc_main_cis_locale_and_single_insta…) · 380 chars\u001b[9;33Hd\u001b[Ccomp_function(stealc_main_cis_locale_and_single_insta…) · 4963 chars\u001b[11;1H\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Elara)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                             \r\n\u001b[97mAll static IsDebuggerPresent/QPC xrefs are confined to CRT functions. But the sample resolves APIs dynamically\r\n(LoadLibraryA/GetProcAddress), so anti-analysis could hide behind the encrypted string table. Let me \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97mcheck the\r\nstring-\u001b[Cable question thr\u001b[Cad and\u001b[Csearch for relevant decoded str\u001b[Cng\u001b[2C\u001b[39m                                         \r\n                                                                                                              \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Elara) · ▸ follow_link(#q-string-table) · 1017 chars\u001b[18;30Hsearch\u001b[Cforum(CreateMutex G\u001b[CtUserDefaultLangID keyboa…) · 3019 chars\u001b[20;19HAm\u001b[Clthea) · ▸ decomp_function(init_rc4_keys_and_decrypt_api_names) · 18732 chars\u001b[22;1H○\u001b[17CEl\u001b[Cra) · ▸ rea\u001b[C_me\u001b[Cory(fam\u001b[Cly-\u001b[2Ctel-stealc-v1-v2) · …running\u001b[39m                    \u001b[24;59H       \u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠼ \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90mThinking…\u001b[4;1H\u001b[39m                                                                                                                      \u001b[24;77H \u001b[3