[0.028, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Europa) · ▸ list_strings(60) · 5845 chars\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                             \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Europa) · ▸ list_strings(chrome) · 120 chars\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                          \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Europa) · ▸ list_strings(cmd) · 209 chars\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                         \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Europa) · ▸ list_strings(Internet) · 573 chars\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                            \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Callisto)\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97mAll verified. Let me grab the config-parser address, then post evidence.\u001b[15;19H\u001b[90mCallisto)\u001b[C·\u001b[C▸ get_function(c2_config_parse_flags_browsers_plugins_…) · 350 chars\u001b[17;1H\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Callisto) · ▸ get_function(http_download_url_to_file) · 314 chars\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                        \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Developer(Ganymede)\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97mAt\u001b[93m 0x14007d6e0\u001b[97m sits the key literal\u001b[93m CgeOvEO7hu\u001b[97m itself (byte-level re-read:\u001b[93m 43 67 65 4f 76 45 4f 37 68 75\u001b[97m =\r\n\"CgeOvEO7hu\"), independently confirming the key recovered from the decompile. The one spurious pair was the key-init\r\nblock decoding the key against itself — so\u001b[1m 276 genuine table entries\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m. Now let me post the findings.\u001b[24;62H\u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠹\u001b[34;69H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90m21\u001b[2C83\u001b[10C4\u001b[C921\u001b[12C282\u001b[C758\u001b[7C8503\u001b[26;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[4;1H \u001b[C                                                         \r\n\u001b[93mEvidence / verification by two independent routes:\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                            \r\n\u001b[93m- Decompile route: init_rc4_keys_and_decrypt_api_names @ 0x140001ee0 stores the literal \"CgeOvEO7hu\" (len 10) into the\r\nglobal key std::string at\u001b[1m 0x1400b0b30\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (len @ 0x1400b0b40, cap @ 0x1400b0b48), which rc4_decrypt_with_global_key reads\r\nfor every KSA. The same function stores a 16-hex-char build/campaign ID \"512e7bd984984fb6\" into 0x1400b05f0.\r\n- Byte-level route: read(0x14007d6e0, 16) = 43 67 65 4f 76 45 4f 37 68 75 = CgeOvEO7hu raw in .rdata.\r\n- Plaintext cross-check against known constant tables: decoding with this key yields exact WinAPI export names across\r\n100+ entries (GetProcAddress, GdipDisposeImage, RegQueryValueExA, GetLogicalProcessorInformationEx, ...) — impossible\r\nby chance with a wrong key.\u001b[39m                     "]
[0.000, "o", "                        \r\n\u001b[93m- Sanity check with the native tool: decode_bytes(\"/x6mNTpQ8CGGjZQ=\", [base64, rc4(\"CgeOvEO7hu\")]) → 45.93.20.28 (the\r\nC2 IP, stored at 0x1400b0490).\u001b[39m                                                                    \u001b[17;1H\u001b[93mThis layout (single global printable RC4 key next to a 16-hex build ID, base64+RC4 string table, x64 MSVC) matches\r\nmemory family-intel-stealc-v1-v2 →\u001b[1m Stealc V2\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m string obfuscation. Decoded all entries with session script\r\ndecode_string_table (args: {\"key\":\"CgeOvEO7hu\",\"funcs\":[\"0x140001ee0\",\"0x140002b6c\"]}), which pairs each ciphertext\r\nxref with th\u001b[C following global-slot\u001b[Cxr\u001b[Cf in address order:\u001b[1m 276 entries decoded, 0 failures\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (one\u001b[Cadditional spurious\r\npair is the key literal itself being paired with the key-slot write at 0x1400b0b3a; excluded). Full list in follow-up\r\ncomments.\u001b[39m                                                                                          \u001b[24;62H    \u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠹ \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90mThinking…\u001b[39m \u001b[35m\u001b[1mDeveloper(Ganymede)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[37m: calling crea\u001b[Ce_comment\u001b[26;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
