[0.000, "o", "\u001b[93mF0003 /*EVENT_ALL_ACCESS*/,\r\nname=ComputerName+UserName)) { CloseHandle; Sleep; } then CreateEventW; ExitProcess(0) on failure.\r\n\u001b[94m6.\u001b[93m\u001b[1m Build-expiry date kill-switch\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m: build_expiry_date_string_from_table @\u001b[1m 0x14002a4c0\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (concatenates 4 decrypted\r\nstring-table entries into a date string) → stealc_main_operation @\u001b[1m 0x14002a774\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m, which parses it via\r\nparse_expiry_date_pct_d_m_Y @\u001b[1m 0x14002a298\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m using format \"%d/%m/%Y\" (day/month/year — literal confirmed both in decompile\r\nand by raw byte read: ASCII 25 64 2f 25 6d 2f 25 59 at file offset 0x80698) and compares mktime(expiry) < mktime(now).\r\nParse failure → ExitProcess(0).\r\n\u001b[94m7. \u001b[93mIf \u001b[1mnot expired\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m → stealc_orchestrator_collect_exfil_selfdelete @ \u001b[1m0x140029f68\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (the entire payload; next comment).\r\n\u001b[94m8. \u001b[93mCloseHandle(event), dtors, return 0.\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                          \r\n\u001b[93mNote:\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[93m stealc_main_operation's return value true = \"expiry date is in the past\"; the orchestrator only runs on false.\u001b[24;59H\u001b[39m \u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠙ \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90mThinking…\u001b[39m \u001b[35m\u001b[1mReverseEngin\u001b[Cer(C\u001b[2Clisto)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[37m: ca\u001b[Cling create_comment\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
