[0.000, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[94m6\u001b[C\u001b[93m\u001b[1m Build-expiry date kill-switch\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m: build_expiry_date_string_from_table @\u001b[1m 0x14002a4c0\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (concatenates 4 decrypted\r\nstring-table entries into a date string) → stealc_main_operation @\u001b[1m 0x14002a774\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m, which parses it via\r\nparse_expiry\u001b[Cd\u001b[Cte\u001b[Cpct_d_m_Y @\u001b[1m 0x14002a298\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m using\u001b[Cformat \"%d/%m/%Y\"\u001b[C(day/month/year —\u001b[Cliteral confirmed\u001b[Cboth\u001b[Ci\u001b[2Cdecompile\r\nand by raw byte read: ASCII 25 64 2f 25 6d 2f 25 59 at file offset 0x80698) and compares mktime(expiry) < mktime(now).\r\nParse failure → ExitProcess(0).\r\n\u001b[94m7. \u001b[93mIf \u001b[1mnot expired\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m → stealc_orchestrator_collect_exfil_selfdelete @ \u001b[1m0x140029f68\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (the entire payload; next comment).\u001b[39m \r\n\u001b[94m8. \u001b[93mCloseHandle(event), dtors, return 0.\u001b[39m                                                                               \r\n                                                "]
[0.001, "o", "                                                              \r\n\u001b[93mNote: stealc_main_operation's return value true = \"expiry date is in the past\"; the orchestrator only runs on false.\u001b[14;1H\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Developer(Sinope)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                           \r\n\u001b[97mBoth scans succeeded:\u001b[1m 270 decoded strings\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m, and the keyword audit gives explicit per-keyword counts. Before posting,\r\nI'll harden the negative: (a) re-run the keyword audit at minlen 4 to cover short tokens, (b) independently verify key\r\ndecodes via the pure-Rhai\u001b[93m b64rc4\u001b[97m (second decode route, not the native pipeline), and (c) grep the raw file for\r\n\u001b[3mplaintext\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m persistence keywords so the absence claim covers unencrypted strings too.\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                       \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mDeveloper(Sinope)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90m · ▸ run_script(persist_kw_grep) · 878 chars\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                       \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mDeveloper(Sinope) · ▸ run_script(b64rc4) · 1082 chars\u001b[26;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
