[0.096, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[93mC:\\Windows\\system32\\cmd.exe /c timeout /t 5 & del /f /q \"<self>\" → ExitProcess(0).\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                           \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mWorker threads: none.\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m find_func\u001b[2Con *\u001b[Chread* returns\u001b[Conly CRT locale/\u001b[Cnit-thread library functions; there is no\r\nCreateThread/CreateRemoteThread-based worker. All stages run sequentially on the main thread; the only concurrency\r\nprimitive is the QueueUserAPC early-bird injection into a\u001b[Csuspended browser process.\u001b[1m Persistence: none\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (con\u001b[Cistent with\r\nth\u001b[C non-\u001b[2Csident d\u001b[Csign; self-\u001b[Celet\u001b[C instead).\u001b[39m                                                                    \r\n                                                                                                                       \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Developer(Sinope)\u001b(B\u001b[m                          \r\n\u001b[97mStrong results: the full table is\u001b[1m 276 strings\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m at minlen 4 (matching the known-complete table), still zero persistence\r\nhits; the pure-Rhai RC4 route byte-matches the native decode; and the only \"timeout/del\" in the whole file is a\r\n\u001b[1mplaintext\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m li\u001b[Ceral\u001b[93m /c timeout /t 5 & del /f /q \"\u001b[97m at file\u001b[C0x8191b (≈ VA 0x14008271b, .rda\u001b[2C) — the se\u001b[Cf-delet\u001b[C comma\u001b[Cd,\r\nou\u001b[2Cide the encrypted table. Let me tie tha\u001b[C literal to its consumer and (bonus for #q-string-table) recover the\r\nglobal-storag\u001b[C mapping with the proven\u001b[93m rc4_b64_strings\u001b[97m.\u001b[39m                                                              \r\n                                                                                                         