[0.001, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[93mbut th\u001b[Cse are in the c\u001b[Cear):\u001b[39m                                                                                        \r\n                                                                                                          \r\n\u001b[93m- C:\\builder_v2\\stealc\\js\u001b[Cn.h @ 0x14007f550\u001b[C— Stealc v2 bu\u001b[2Cder\u001b[Cp\u001b[Cth (f\u001b[Cmily tell)\u001b[39m                   \r\n\u001b[93m- uFL7eGwTnXjG2cMD5M2m @ 0x14007f0a0 — 20-char high-entropy token in .rdata; prime candidate for the\u001b[1m global RC4 key\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m of\r\nthe string table (family intel says v2 uses a single global RC4 key) → verify in #q-string-table\r\n- WinINet API names (runtime-resolved C2 capability): InternetOpenW, InternetConnectW, HttpOpenRequestW,\u001b[39m              \r\n\u001b[93mHttpSendRequestW, InternetReadFile, InternetCloseHandle, InternetOpenUrlA @ 0x140082770–0x1400827f8\r\n- C:\\Windows\\system32\\cmd.exe @ 0x140082740 — fits the self-delete cmd /c timeout ... del routine (#fn-14003b870,\r\n#q-persistence)\u001b[39m                                                                                \r\n\u001b[93m- \\\\.\\pipe\\ @ 0x140080dd0 — named-pipe prefix (possible child-process output capture / sRDI DLL comms)\r\n- \\Google\\Chrome\\User Data\\Local State @ 0x1400a8208 (.data) — Chrome targeting, fits the embedded sRDI ABE-bypass DLL\r\n(programs embedded_srdi_dll / abe_sRDI_blob already imported in this project)\r\n- nlohmann/json diagnostic strings + standard base64 alphabet @ 0x140080e40 (noted by detector) — used by the b64+RC4\r\npipeline\r\n- MSVC/UCRT internals (minkernel\\crts\\ucrt\\inc\\corecrt_internal_strtox.h, 1#QNAN-class CRT noise) — ignore per pitfall\r\nmemories.\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                             \r\n\u001b[93mAlso note: this project already contains two imported child programs (embedded_srdi_dll, abe_sRDI_blob, 549