[0.003, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[94m4.\u001b[93m Emb\u001b[Cdded sRDI\u001b[CABE-byp\u001b[Css DLL: project contains imported children embedded_srdi_dll / abe_sRDI_blob, injected by\r\ninject_abe_helper_blob_QueueUserAPC @ 0x14003a048 (early-bird QueueUserAPC into suspended browser) from the Chromium\r\ncollector @ 0x14001f100 — V2's signature Chrome v20 key\u001b[Ctheft.\u001b[39m                    \r\n\u001b[94m5.\u001b[93m Stealer behavior chain in orchestrator @ 0x140029f68: s\u001b[Cs\u001b[Cem info\u001b[Creport,\u001b[CChromium/F\u001b[Crefox p\u001b[Cofile theft,\u001b[39m          \r\n\u001b[93mconfig-driven file grabber, Steam theft, screenshot,\u001b[Cchunked base64-JSON ex\u001b[Cil over HTTP (c2_http_post_json @\r\n0x14000b384).\u001b[39m                                                                                           \r\n\u001b[94m6.\u001b[93m Loader capability = C2 task dispatch @ 0x140029900 with exactly the V2\u001b[Ctask triad: EXE (ShellExecuteExA, optional\r\nrunas), P\u001b[2CerS\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93mhell IEX one-liner, MSI via msiexec.\u001b[39m                                                               \r\n\u001b[94m7.\u001b[93m CIS LANGID kill-gate (0x419/0x422/0x423/0x43F/0x443), named-EVENT single-instance gate,\u001b[1m no persistence\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m, flag-gated\r\nself-delete\u001b[C(cmd /c timeout\u001b[C/t 5 & del\u001b[C/f /q \"<self>\" @\u001b[C0x14003b870) — non-resident stealer\u001b[Cdesign.\u001b[39m   \r\n\u001b[94m8.\u001b[93m\u001b[1m Ransomware refuted\u001b[C\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93mfor the \"Data Encrypted for Impact\" detecto\u001b[C flags: the only crypto\u001b[Cis RC4 string\u001b[Cdecryption\u001b[Cof\u001b[39m \r\n\u001b[93mthe binary's own string table\u001b[2Cnd base64 encodings for C2; there is no file-encryption loop and no victim-file\r\nenumeration feeding an en\u001b[Cryptor (flags match\u001b[Cpitfall pitfall-t1486-flags-from-c2-rc4-and-sandbox-dir-coun\u001b[Cing; the\u001b[39m  \r\n\u001b[93m16/32-byte \"keys\" in #fn-140002b6c are encrypted string-table entries per\r\npitfall-carved-b64-keys-are-e\u001b[Ccrypted-st\u001b[Cings).\u001b[39m                                                                       \r\n         \r\n\u001b[93mOne deviation from the previously-memorized V2 build:\u001b[1m this build HAS a build-expiry date kill-switch\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (\"%d/%m/%Y\" parse\r\n@ 0x14002a298, compare vs current time @\u001b[C0x14002a774,\u001b[Cpay\u001b[Coad skipped if \u001b[Cxpired) — a V1\u001b[Cfeature the earlier-a\u001b[Calyzed\u001b[39m  \r\n\u001b[93mbuild\u001b[Clacke\u001b[C. Field order\u001b[Cday/month/year verif\u001b[Ced\u001b[Cbyte-level (ASCII %d/%m/%Y at file off\u001b[Ce\u001b[C 0x80698).\u001b[39m           \u001b[24;60H\u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠙ \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90mThinking…\u001b[39m \u001b[35m\u001b[1mRev\u001b[CrseEngineer(Callisto\u001b[26;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.016, "o", "\u001b[4;1H                                                                                                                  \r\n\u001b[93mDecompiled, the who\u001b[Ce function is:\u001b[39m                                                                                  \r\n                                                              \r\n\u001b[93m```c\u001b[39m                                                                                                        \r\n\u001b[38;5;251mundefined8 * \u001b[38;5;109mbad_array_new_length_ctor\u001b[38;5;251m(undefined8 *\u001b[38;5;131mparam_1\u001b[38;5;251m) {\u001b[39m                                                \r\n\u001b[38;5;251m  param_1[\u001b[38;5;173m2\u001b[38;5;251m] = \u001b[38;5;173m0\u001b[38;5;251m;\r\n  param_1[\u001b[38;5;173m1\u001b[38;5;251m] = \"\u001b[38;5;144mbad array new length\u001b[38;5;251m\";\u001b[39m                                                                              \r\n\u001b[38;5;251m  *param_1 = &PTR_FUN_140073218;   \u001b[38;5;243m// vtable\u001b[39m      \r\n\u001b[38;5;251m  \u001b[38;5;139mreturn\u001b[38;5;251m param_1;\u001b[39m                                                                                                    \r\n\u001b[38;5;251m}\u001b[39m                                                                                                  \r\n\u001b[93m```\u001b[39m                                                                                                                  \r\n                                                                                                              \r\n\u001b[93mIt is the MSVC std::bad_ar\u001b[Cay_new_len\u001b[Cth ex\u001b[Cept\u001b[Con-objec\u001b[C cons\u001b[Cructor — no crypto, no data transformati\u001b[Cn at all.\u001b[39m  \r\n                                                                         \r\n\u001b[93mThe three detector findings (repea\u001b[Cing-XOR key \"address in use\" over .rdata at 0x140075071/0x14007507d/0x14007509d\r\nyielding garbage like efwasmk!a{) are the known false-positive class from memory\r\npitfall-detecto\u001b[C-xor-keys-fr\u001b[Cm-crt-symbol-strings: \"address in use\"is a CRT/STLerrc` message string sitting in the CRT\r\nerror-message table in\u001b[C.rdata, and XORing it against neighboring message\u001b[Cbytes produces unprintable junk. Garbage\u001b[39m    \r\n\u001b[93m\"plaintext\" =\u001b[2CP. No code\u001b[Cxrefs use these bytes as key mat\u001b[Crial.\u001b[39m                                     "]
