[0.002, "o", "\u001b[5;1H\u001b[93m```c\u001b[39m                              \r\n\u001b[38;5;251mundefined8 * \u001b[38;5;109mbad_array_new_length_ctor\u001b[38;5;251m(undefined8 *\u001b[38;5;131mparam_1\u001b[38;5;251m) {\r\n  param_1[\u001b[38;5;173m2\u001b[38;5;251m] = \u001b[38;5;173m0\u001b[38;5;251m;\r\n  param_1[\u001b[38;5;173m1\u001b[38;5;251m]\u001b[C= \"\u001b[38;5;144mbad array new length\u001b[38;5;251m\";\u001b[39m                       \u001b[9;3H\u001b[38;5;251m*param_1 =\u001b[C&PTR_FUN_140073218;   \u001b[38;5;243m// vtable\u001b[10;3H\u001b[38;5;139mreturn\u001b[38;5;251m param_1;\u001b[39m                     \r\n\u001b[38;5;251m}\u001b[39m                                           \r\n\u001b[93m```\u001b[39m              \r\n \r\n\u001b[93mIt is the MSVC std::bad_array_new_length exception-object constructor — no crypto, no data transformation at all.\u001b[16;1HThe thre\u001b[2Cdetector fin\u001b[Cings (repeati\u001b[2C-XOR k\u001b[Cy \"address in use\" over .rdata at 0x140075071/0x14007507d/0x14007509d\r\nyielding garbage like efwasmk!a{) are the known false-positive class from memory\r\npitfall-det\u001b[Cctor-xor-keys-from-crt-symbol-strings: \"address in use\"is a CRT/STLerrc` message string sitting in the CRT\r\nerror-mess\u001b[Cge tab\u001b[Ce in .rdata, and XORing\u001b[Cit against neighboring me\u001b[Csage bytes produces unprintable junk. Garbage\r\n\"plaintext\" = FP. No code x\u001b[Cefs use these bytes as\u001b[Ckey mater\u001b[Cal.\u001b[39m                                                      \r\n                                                                                                                 \r\n\u001b[90m○\u001b[39m \u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Callisto) · ▸ complete_task(main) · …running\u001b[39m  \u001b[24;60H \u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠋ \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90mThinking…\u001b[39m \u001b[35m\u001b[1mReverseEngin\u001b[Cer(Ca\u001b[Clisto)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[37m: ca\u001b[Cling complete_task\u001b[26;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.019, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[38;5;251m  param_1[\u001b[38;5;173m1\u001b[38;5;251m] = \"\u001b[38;5;144mbad array new length\u001b[38;5;251m\";\r\n  *param_1 = &PTR_FUN_140073218;   \u001b[38;5;243m// vtable\r\n\u001b[38;5;251m  \u001b[38;5;139mreturn\u001b[38;5;251m param_1;\u001b[39m                                            \r\n\u001b[38;5;251m}\u001b[39m                \r\n\u001b[93m```\u001b[39m                                   \r\n                                            \r\n\u001b[93mIt is the MSVC std::bad_array_new_length exception-object constructor — no crypto, no data transformation at all.\r\n\u001b[39m \r\n\u001b[93mThe three detector findings (repeating-XOR key \"address in use\" over .rdata at 0x140075071/0x14007507d/0x14007509d\r\nyielding garbage like efwasmk!a{) are the known false-positive class from memory\r\npitfall-detector-xor-keys-from-crt-symbol-strings: \"address in use\"is\u001b[Ca\u001b[CCRT/STLerrc` mess\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[C\u001b[93mge string sitting in the CRT\r\nerror-message table in .rdata, and XORing it against neighboring message bytes produces unprintable junk. Garbage\r\n\"plaint\u001b[Cxt\" = FP. No code xrefs use these bytes \u001b[Cs k\u001b[Cy material.\u001b[39m                                                  \r\n                                                                                \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Callisto) · ▸ complete_task(main) · 211 chars\u001b[39m                                                       \r\n                                                                                                                 \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Callisto) · ▸ complete_task(main) · 187 chars\u001b[39m \u001b[22;1H\u001b[32m●\u001b[53C\u001b[90m198 chars\u001b[26;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
