[0.014, "o", "\u001b[4;20H\u001b[90mlara) · ▸ read(14003c160) · 96\u001b[Cchars\u001b[39m      \u001b[6;19H\u001b[90mCallisto)\u001b[C·\u001b[C▸ set_s\u001b[Catus(#q-m\u001b[Cin-flow) · 10390 chars\u001b[8;1H\u001b[93m📌 #finding-expiry-date-killswitch — Build-expiry date kill-switch present in this Stealc V2 build (%d/%m/%Y)\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEng\u001b[9;1H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93mThis build gates the entire payload behind a \u001b[1mbuild-expiry date check\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m in WinMain (@ 0x14002a88c):\u001b[39m                 \r\n                                                                                \r\n\u001b[93m- build_expiry_date_string_from_table @ 0x14002a4c0 concatenates\u001b[1m 4 decrypted string-table entries\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (DAT_1400b09f0,\r\nDAT_1400b0e90, DAT_1400b1ab0, DAT_1400b1e10) via a stringstream into the expiry-date string (so the concrete date needs\r\nthe decoded table — see #q-string-table).\r\n- stealc_main_operation @ 0x14002a774: current time (_Xtime_get_ticks → localtime) vs the parsed date; parse via\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n\u001b[93mparse_expiry_date_pct_d_m_Y @ 0x14002a298 with format literal \"%d/%m/%Y\" (\u001b[1mday/month/year\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m; verified in decompile AND raw\r\nbytes 25 64 2f 25 6d 2f 25 59 @ file offset 0x80698). Parse failure → ExitProcess(0).\r\n- Returns mktime(expiry) < mktime(now); if true (expired), WinMain\u001b[1m skips\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m stealc_orchestrator_collect_exfil_selfdelete @\r\n0x140029f68 entirely and exits cleanly.\u001b[39m                        \u001b[20;1H\u001b[93mNote for memory curation: family-intel-stealc-v1-v2 says the 2025-04 verified V2 build had\u001b[1m no\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m date kill-switch; this\r\nbuild\u001b[1m has one\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (V1 feature retained/re-enabled). Anti-sandbox/anti-analysis relevance: run-date rolls past expiry ⇒\r\nsample looks benign in detonation.\u001b[39m                                 \u001b[24;63H\u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠼ \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90mThinking…\u001b[39m \u001b[35m\u001b[1mReverseEngine\u001b[Cr(Cal\u001b[Cisto)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[37m: cal\u001b[Cing cr\u001b[Cate_post\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
