[0.003, "o", "\u001b[4;1H \u001b[C                                              \r\n\u001b[93m- InternetConnectW slot (DAT_1400b4d88) is called only from c2_http_pos\u001b[C_j\u001b[Con and http_download_url_to_file; the\u001b[39m    \r\n\u001b[93mformer's host argument always comes from DAT_1400b0490 at every xref'd caller (0x140029b6d, \u001b[Cx14000acec, 0x140026c6e,\r\n0\u001b[C1400266b8, 0x14000caef).\r\n- http_download_url_to_file (loader path) takes its URL from the C2 \"loader\" task response — dynamic, not embedded.\u001b[9;3HNo oth\u001b[Cr decoded\u001b[2Ctring-table entry sampled so far is a host/URL; the complete table \u001b[Cecode (open in #q-string-table)\r\nis the remaining cross-check — follow-up\u001b[Cthere should flag any additional host-shaped plainte\u001b[Cts.\u001b[39m                    \r\n                          \r\n\u001b[93mResidual u\u001b[Cverified deta\u001b[2C (low impact): two further C2\u001b[CPOST\u001b[Cbuilders exist — FUN_140026a84 and FUN_14000b690 — both\r\nusing \u001b[3C same DAT_1400b0490/0630 host+gate and the same base64(JSON) shape (xr\u001b[Cfs confirm); their exact type verbs\u001b[39m    \r\n\u001b[93m(likely the sysinfo/\u001b[Ccreenshot\u001b[Creport messages) were not decompiled before context ran out.\u001b[39m      \u001b[16;1H\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Elara) · ▸ decode_bytes([{\"op\":\"base64\"},{\"op\":\"rc4\",\"key\":\"Cge…) · 201 chars\u001b[39m                     \r\n                                                                                                                   \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Elara) · ▸ get_function(0x14003ef98) · 270 chars\u001b[39m                         \u001b[20;1H\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Callisto)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                   \r\n\u001b[97m#q-main-flow is now solved. Let me add brief cross-reference comments to the related open questions that my trace\r\ndirectly informs.\u001b[39m                                                 \u001b[24;60H\u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠼ \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90mThinking…\u001b[39m \u001b[35m\u001b[1mRevers\u001b[CEngineer(Callisto)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[37m: calling crea\u001b[Ce_comment\u001b[26;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.001, "o", "\u001b[5;1H\u001b[93mResidual unverified de\u001b[Cail (low impact\u001b[C: two further C2 POST builders exist —\u001b[CFUN_140026a84 an\u001b[C FUN\u001b[C14000b690 — both\r\nusing the same DAT_1400b0490/0630 host+gate and the same bas\u001b[C64(JSON) sh\u001b[Cpe (xrefs confirm); their exa\u001b[Ct\u001b[Ctype verbs\u001b[39m  \r\n\u001b[93m(likely the sysinfo/screenshot report messages) were not decompiled before context ran out.\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                   \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Elara) · ▸ decode_bytes([{\"op\":\"base64\"},{\"op\":\"rc4\",\"key\":\"Cge…) · 201 chars\u001b[39m                        \r\n                                                                                                 \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Elara) · ▸ get_function(0x14003ef98) · 270 chars\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                    \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Callisto)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                                       \r\n\u001b[97m#q-main-flow is now solved. Let me add brief cross-reference comments to the related open questions that my trace\r\ndirectly informs.\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                                                             \r\n\u001b[93m💬 reply #q-persistence\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Callisto)\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93mFrom the main-flow trace (!56, !60):\u001b[1m no persistence mechanism exists\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m — no registry Run key, scheduled task, service, or\r\nstartup-folder code anywhere in the top-level flow; the design is non-resident (Stealc V2). Self-deletion:\r\nself_delete_cmd_timeout_del_shellexecute @ 0x14003b870, invoked at the end of the orchestrator @ 0x140029f68\u001b[1m only if a\r\nC2-config flag (struct offset +0x40, 'self_delete') is set\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m. Mechanism: GetModuleFileNameA(NULL) → ShellExecuteExA\r\nC:\\Windows\\system32\\cmd.exe with args /c timeout /t 5 & del /f /q \"<own path>\" → ExitProcess(0).\u001b[26;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.020, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[94m1.\u001b[93m\u001b[1m CIS locale kill-gate\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m — GetUserDefaultLangID vs 0x419/0x422/0x423/0x43F/0x443 (ru/uk/be/kk/uz-Latn) → ExitProcess(0).\r\nVictim-geofenc\u001b[Cng, not sandbox detection.\u001b[39m                                                                           \r\n\u001b[94m2. \u001b[93m\u001b[1mNamed-event single-instance gate\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m — OpenEve\u001b[CtW poll loop on event name Comput\u001b[CrName+UserName, then Crea\u001b[CeEventW.\u001b[39m \r\n\u001b[94m3.\u001b[93m\u001b[1m Build-expiry date kill-switch\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m — see #finding-expiry-dat\u001b[C-killswitch (%d/%m/%Y @\u001b[C0x14002a298; expired ⇒ payload\r\nskipped). Causes benign-looking detonations after the expiry date.\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                                                             \r\n\u001b[93mNo VM/debugger/sandbox checks appear anywhere in the top-level flow (IsDebuggerPresent occurrences are static-CRT\r\nnoise). Obfuscation-side anti-analysis = base64+RC4 string table (0x140002b6c) + runtime API resolution\r\n(0x14003c0a8/0x14003c2ac) keeping the static import table clean.\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                          \r\n\u001b[93m💬 reply #q-ransomware\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Callisto)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                 \r\n\u001b[93mMain-flow trace evidence\u001b[1m against\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m ransomware (details in !60/!65 under #q-main-flow): the complete top-level call graph\r\nfrom WinMain @ 0x14002a88c through the orchestrator @ 0x140029f68 contains\u001b[1m no file-encryption component\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m — every stage\r\nis\u001b[Cstealer/loader fu\u001b[2Ctionality (string decrypt, API resolve, C2 register+config, browser/Firefox/Steam/grabber\r\ncollection, screenshot, chunked base64-JSON exfil, task dispatch exe/ps1/msi, \u001b[Celf-delet\u001b[C).\u001b[CThe T1486\u001b[Cdetector flags\u001b[39m   \r\n\u001b[93mmap \u001b[Co kn\u001b[Cwn FP classes: RC4\u001b[2Cs\u001b[Cus\u001b[Cd \u001b[Cnly to decrypt the binary'\u001b[2Cow\u001b[C str\u001b[Cng \u001b[Cable\u001b[39m                        \r\n\u001b[93m(pitfal\u001b[C-\u001b[C1486-flags-from-c2-rc4-and-sandbox-dir-counting), an\u001b[2Cthe carve\u001b[2C16/32-byte \"AES keys\"\u001b[Cin #fn-140002b6c sit\u001b[39m \r\n\u001b[93minside the encrypted string table itself (pitfall-carved-b64-keys-are-encrypted-strings). Classification:\u001b[1m Stealc V2\r\ninfostealer\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m, hard tell C:\\builder_v2\\stealc\\json.h @ file offset 0x7e756.\u001b[39m                       \u001b[26;2H"]
