[0.001, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[94m2\u001b[C \u001b[93m\u001b[1mNamed-event single-instance gate\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m — OpenEventW poll loop on event name ComputerName+Us\u001b[CrName, the\u001b[C CreateEventW.\u001b[39m     \r\n\u001b[94m3.\u001b[93m\u001b[1m Build-expiry date kill-switch\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m — see #finding-expiry-date-killswitch (%d/%m/%Y @ 0x14002a298; expired ⇒ payload\r\nskipped). Causes benign-looking detonatio\u001b[Cs af\u001b[Cer the\u001b[Cexpiry dat\u001b[C.\u001b[39m                                                \r\n                                                                                                                 \r\n\u001b[93mNo VM/\u001b[Cebugger/\u001b[Candbox chec\u001b[Cs app\u001b[Car \u001b[Cnywhere in the top-level flow (IsDebuggerPresent occurrences are static-CRT\r\nnoise). Obfuscation-side anti-analysis = base64+RC4 string table (0x140002b6c) + runtime API resolution\r\n(0x14003c0a8/0x14003c2a\u001b[C) keeping the static import table cl\u001b[Can.\u001b[39m                                                 \r\n                                                                                                       \r\n\u001b[93m💬 reply #q-ransomware\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Callisto)\u001b(B\u001b[m                \r\n\u001b[93mMain-flow trace evidence\u001b[1m against\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m ransomware (details in !60/!65 under #q-main-flow): the complete top-level call graph\r\nfrom WinMain @ 0x14002a88c through the orchestrator @ 0x140029f68 contains\u001b[1m no file-encryption component\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m — every stage\r\nis stealer/loader functionality (string decrypt, API\u001b[Cresolve, C2 register+co\u001b[Cfig, brows\u001b[Cr/Firefox/Steam/grabber\u001b[39m       \r\n\u001b[93mcollection, screenshot, chunked base64-JSON exfil, task dispatch exe/ps1/msi, self-delete). The T1486 detecto\u001b[C flags\u001b[39m \r\n\u001b[93mmap \u001b[Co known FP classes: RC4 is\u001b[Cu\u001b[Ced only to decrypt\u001b[Cthe binary's own st\u001b[Cing table\u001b[39m                             \r\n\u001b[93m(pitfall-t1486-flags-from-c2-rc4-\u001b[Cnd-sandbox-dir-counting), \u001b[Cnd the carved 16/32-byt\u001b[C \"AES keys\" in #fn-140002b6c sit\r\ninside\u001b[Cthe encrypted string table itself (pitfall-carved-\u001b[C64-key\u001b[C-are-encrypted-strings). Classification:\u001b[1m Stealc V2\r\ninfostealer\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m, hard tell C:\\builder_v2\\\u001b[Ctealc\\json.h @ f\u001b[Cle offset 0x7e756.\u001b[39m                                            \r\n                                                                                                                   \r\n\u001b[90m○\u001b[39m \u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Amalthea) · ▸ complete_task(reverse-engineer) · …running\u001b[24;60H\u001b[39m \u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠦ \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90mThinking…\u001b[39m \u001b[35m\u001b[1mReverseEngin\u001b[Cer(Amalthea)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[37m: ca\u001b[Cling complete_task\u001b[26;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.021, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[93mNo VM/debugger/sandbox checks appear anywher\u001b[C in\u001b[Cthe top-level flow\u001b[C(IsDebuggerP\u001b[Cesent occurr\u001b[Cnces are static-CRT\u001b[39m \r\n\u001b[93mnoise). Obfuscation-side anti-analy\u001b[Cis\u001b[C= base64+RC4 string tab\u001b[Ce (0x140002b6c) +\u001b[Cruntime API resolution\u001b[39m          \r\n\u001b[93m(0x14003c0a8/0x14003c2ac) keeping \u001b[Che static impor\u001b[C table clean.\u001b[39m  \u001b[8;1H\u001b[93m💬\u001b[Creply #q-ran\u001b[Comware\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Callisto)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                 \r\n\u001b[93mMa\u001b[Cn-flow tra\u001b[Ce evidenc\u001b[C\u001b[1m against\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m ransomware (details in !60/!65 under #q-main-flow): th\u001b[2Ccompl\u001b[Cte top-level call graph\r\nfrom WinMain @ 0x1400\u001b[2C88c throu\u001b[Ch the orchestrator\u001b[C@ 0x140029f68 contains\u001b[1m no file-encryption component\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m — every stage\r\nis stealer/loader functionality (string decrypt, API resolve, C2 register+config, browser/Firefox/Steam/grabber\r\ncoll\u001b[Cction, screenshot, chunked base64-JSON exfil, task dispatch exe/ps1/msi, self-delete). The T1486 detector flags\r\nm\u001b[Cp to known FP\u001b[Cclasses: RC4 is used \u001b[Cnly to \u001b[2Ccrypt\u001b[Cthe binary's own\u001b[Cstring table\u001b[39m                                    \r\n\u001b[93m(pitfall-t1486-flags-from-c2-\u001b[Cc4-and-sandbox-dir-counting), and the carved 16/32-byte \"AES keys\" in #fn-140002b6c sit\u001b[15;2Hnsid\u001b[C the encrypted s\u001b[Cri\u001b[Cg table itself (pitfall-carv\u001b[Cd-b64-keys-are-encrypted-string\u001b[C). Classification:\u001b[1m Stealc V2\r\ninfostealer\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m, hard tell C:\\buil\u001b[Cer_v2\\stealc\\json.h\u001b[C@ file offset\u001b[C0\u001b[C7e756.\u001b[39m                                           \r\n                                                           