[0.002, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[93m```\u001b[39m                                              \r\n \r\n\u001b[93mSlot→API identities, each verified by decrypting the name literal fed to the GetProcAddress call that produced the slot\r\nvalue (base64+RC4, key CgeOvEO7hu):\r\n\u001b[39m   \r\n\u001b[93m- 0x1400b4e28 ← hFvtYkwIp3/c6A== = \u001b[1mOpenEventW\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (resolved @ 0x14003c1c6)\r\n- 0x1400b4e30 ← \u001b[CFntbX0b\u001b[C2fN0dh6 =\u001b[C\u001b[1mCreateEventW\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (@ 0x14003c1f1)\u001b[39m                                                        \r\n\u001b[93m- 0x1400b4\u001b[C38 ← mEftaXk= = \u001b[1mSleep\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (@ 0x14003c21c)\r\n- 0x1400b4d58 ← iEfnf2w2o3/M08k= = \u001b[1mCloseHandle\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (@ 0x14003c176)\u001b[13;12Ha0\u001b[3CjE78T2YTsmT\u001b[C2t5j8di3fA== = \u001b[1mGetComputerNameW\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (@ \u001b[Cx14003c247)\r\n\u001b[39m                                                               \r\n\u001b[93mBehavior: if another instance already holds the event, the new instance polls every ~4.1 s until it disappears, then\r\ncreates the event a\u001b[Cd pr\u001b[Cceeds. CreateMutex/OpenMutex do NOT exist anywhere: not in the static import table and not in\r\nthe encrypted\u001b[Cstring table (searched for\u001b[Ctheir deterministic RC4-ciphertext base64 prefixes iFntbX0bj2Tc / hFvtYkQL —\r\nzero hits). The Sleep(0x100A) loop is an instance-wait, not a sandbox timing evasion.\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                    \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Researcher(Lysithea)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                                               \r\n\u001b[97mThe memory is amended. Now I'll record the curation action on the forum thread, plus one bonus inference the RE team\u001b[39m \r\n\u001b[97mmay want to confirm.\u001b[39m                                                                 \u001b[26;2H"]
[0.002, "o", "\u001b[4;1H   \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Researcher(Lysithea)\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97mThe memory is amended. Now I'll record the curation action on the forum thread, plus one bonus inference the RE team\u001b[39m   \r\n\u001b[97mmay want to confirm.\u001b[39m               \u001b[9;1H\u001b[93m💬 reply #finding-expiry-date-killswitch\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Researcher(Lysithea)\u001b(B\u001b[m         \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mMemory library updated\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m per this finding: family-intel-stealc-v1-v2 has been amended (overwrite). The old line\r\n\"[VERIFIED v2\u001b[Cbuild] NO build-expiry date kill-switch in this build (a v1 feature apparently dropped)\" is replaced by a\r\n\u001b[1m[PER-BUILD]\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m item stating the expiry gate is builder-configurable in V2 — present in this build ([binary fact], !56 +\r\nthis post), absent in the earlier 2025-04 build — with a generic per-sample check recipe (grep ASCII %d/%m/%Y; find the\r\nWinMain-level 4-entry stringstream concatenation; find the mktime comparison gating the orchestrator) and the\r\nanti-sandbox\u001b[Cnote that post-\u001b[Cxpi\u001b[Cy \u001b[Cetonations look benign\u001b[C(consider \u001b[Clock backdating)\u001b[C The diagnostic-combo \u001b[Cec\u001b[Cio\r\nnow explicitly says never to use the gate's pr\u001b[Csenc\u001b[C/absence\u001b[Cas a V2 version\u001b[Cdiscriminator.\u001b[39m                           \r\n                                                                                                                     \r\n\u001b[93mBonus hypothesis for the RE team (needs one che\u001b[Ck): per\u001b[C!59\u001b[Cthe four slots us\u001b[Cd by build_expiry_date_string_from_table\r\n@ 0x14002a4c0 decode to DAT_1400b09f0=\"11\", DAT_1400b0e90=\"04\", DAT_1400b1ab0=\"20\", DAT_1400b1e10=\"25\". If the\r\nstringstream inserts / separators as the %d/%m/%Y format implies, the concrete expiry date of this build is\u001b[1m 11/04/2025\r\n(11 April 2025)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m — i.e. the sample has already expired on any current-clock detonation. Worth confirming the separator\r\ninsertion in the decompile of 0x14002a4c0 before treating that date as established.\u001b[24;63H\u001b[39m  \u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠦ \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90mThinking…\u001b[39m \u001b[35m\u001b[1mR\u001b[Csearcher(Lysithe\u001b[26;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
