[0.076, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[97m-\u001b[1m Removed\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m the over-generalized claim \"[VERIFIED v2 build] NO build-expiry date kill-switch in this build (a v1 feature\r\napparently dropped)\".\u001b[39m                                                                               \r\n\u001b[97m-\u001b[1m Added\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m a new\u001b[1m [PER-BUILD]\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m marker convention: the memory now notes it is verified against\u001b[3m two\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m real V2 builds, and items\r\nwhere builds differ are flagged per-build.\u001b[39m                                                                   \r\n\u001b[97m-\u001b[1m New expiry-gate item\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m: the build-expiry date kill-switch is\u001b[1m builder-configurable in V2\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m — absent in the 2025-04 build\r\n(build A),\u001b[1m present\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m in the current build (build B). It records the generic implementation pattern (WinMain-level helper\r\nconcatenating 4 small 2-char decrypted string-table entries via stringstream →\u001b[C\u001b[93mstd:\u001b[Cget_time\u001b[97m with\u001b[93m \"%d/%m/%Y\"\u001b[97m →\r\n\u001b[93mmktime(expiry) < mktime(now)\u001b[97m gating the orchestrator; parse failure →\u001b[C\u001b[93mExitProcess(0)\u001b[97m), a\u001b[1m per-sample check recipe\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (grep\r\n\u001b[93m%d/%m/%Y\u001b[97m in .rdata; find the 4-entry concatenator; find the mktime gate), and the\u001b[1m anti-sandbox note\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m that post-expiry\r\ndetonations look benign — backdate the clock in dynamic analysis.\u001b[39m               \r\n\u001b[97m- \u001b[1mDiagnostic combo section\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m now explicitly warns never to use the gate's presence/absence as a V2 discriminator.\r\n- Description and tags updated (\u001b[93mkill-switch\u001b[97m,\u001b[93m expiry-date\u001b[97m added) so future runs searching for expiry/kill-switch topics\r\nfind it. No sample hashes, addresses, or session-specific IOCs were put in the memory — the concrete evidence stays on\r\nthe forum (#q-main-flow !56, #finding-expiry-date-killswitch).\r\n\u001b[39m   \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mForum record\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (!80 under #finding-expiry-date-killswitch): documented the curation action, and posted one pre-registered\r\nhypothesis for the RE team: the four table entries (\"11\",\"04\",\"20\",\"25\") imply a concrete expiry of\u001b[1m 11 April 2025\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m\u001b[3m if\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93mbuild_expiry_da\u001b[Ce_string_from_table\u001b[97m @ 0x14002a4c0 inserts\u001b[C\u001b[93m/\u001b[97m separators — flagged as needing one decompile check before\r\npromotion to a conclusion.\u001b[24;68H\u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠸\u001b[34;67H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90m133\u001b[2C4\u001b[11C3\u001b[C251\u001b[14C86\u001b[C493\u001b[7C1908\u001b[26;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
