[0.005, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[93m\u001b[1mANSWER — complete enumeration of anti-analysis in this sample (Stealc v2):\u001b(B\u001b[m                                          \r\n                                                                                                                      \r\n\u001b[93mGenuine malware-authored checks (both in stealc_main_cis_locale_and_single_instance_gate @ 0x14002a88c):\u001b[8;1H\u001b[94m1.\u001b[93m\u001b[1m CIS locale kill switch\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m @ 0x14002a96d: runtime-resolved GetUserDefaultLangID() vs 0x419/0x422/0x423/0x43F/0x443\r\n(ru/uk/be/kk/uz-Latn) → ExitProcess(0). Environment keying / geofencing (T1614.001). Evidence: !77.\r\n\u001b[94m2.\u001b[93m\u001b[1m Single-instance gate via named event\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (<numeric>_<ComputerName>_<UserName>): OpenEventW poll loop (CloseHandle +\r\nSleep 4106 ms) then CreateEventW, NULL → ExitProcess(0). Not a mutex. Evidence: !79.\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                          \r\n\u001b[93mEverything else is CRT boilerplate or absent:\u001b[39m                                                                         \r\n                                                                   \r\n\u001b[93m- IsDebuggerPresent ×3, QueryPerformanceCounter ×1, OutputDebugStringW, GetSystemTimeAsFileTime ×2, FindNextFile hits:\r\nall inside identified MSVC runtime functions, unreachable as malware evasion (!75).\r\n- No anti-debug, no anti-VM, no sandbox detection, no timing checks, no mutex: proven by deterministic ciphertext\r\nsearch over the encrypted API-name/string table (!81).\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                       \r\n\u001b[93mSo: the sample's only \"anti-analysis\" is CIS-locale environment keying + a named-event single-instance check, plus the\r\ngeneral obfuscation layer (encrypted string table + runtime API resolution). No build-expiry date kill switch observed\r\neither (GetLocalTime/GetSystemTime absent from kill paths), consistent with the verified v2 build in family intel.\u001b[24;63H\u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠇ \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90mThinking…\u001b[39m \u001b[35m\u001b[1mReverseEngine\u001b[Cr(Elara)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[37m: calling cre\u001b[Cte_comm\u001b[Cnt\u001b[26;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
