[0.003, "o", "\u001b[4;1H                                                                                                                       \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mAbsent (proven, !81):\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m no anti-debug, anti-VM, sandbox detection, or timing checks in malware code — verified by\r\nsearching the encrypted string table for deterministic RC4-ciphertext base64 prefixes of IsDebuggerPresent,\r\nCheckRemoteDebuggerPresent, NtQueryInformationProcess, GetTickCount, QueryPerformanceCounter, VMw\u001b[Cre,\u001b[39m                 \r\n\u001b[97mCreateMutex/OpenMutex (zero hits; m\u001b[Cthod validated on a known\u001b[Cpair).\u001b[39m                                                   \r\n                                                                                                      \r\n\u001b[97mCross-posted the recovered RC4 key/pipeline to #q-string-table (!84) and annotat\u001b[Cd the kill-switch in Ghidra @\r\n0x14002a96d.\u001b[39m                                                                                                        \r\n                            \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Himalia)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                                          \r\n\u001b[97mThe parse function at 0x140025b6\u001b[C writes JSON-config flags to context offsets 0x40–0x44. Let me independently verify\r\nthe key names, especially that global DAT_1400b0cf0 (used for offset +0x40 — the flag the orchestrator tests before\r\ncalling self-delete) is\u001b[93m self_delete\u001b[97m:\u001b[39m                                                                           \r\n                                                                                                           \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Himalia) · ▸ decode_bytes(uE7kalYap33Ny8k=) · 201 chars\u001b[39m                            \r\n                                                                    \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[C\u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Himalia) · ▸ decode_bytes(v0rjaVYNoWPN2sJe+Nqm) · 209 chars\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                              \r\n\u001b[90m○\u001b[39m \u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Himalia) · ▸ decode_bytes(p0TpaGwM) · …running\u001b[24;60H\u001b[39m   \u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠹ \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90mTh\u001b[2Cking…\u001b[39m \u001b[35m\u001b[1mRev\u001b[CrseE\u001b[Cgineer(Him\u001b[Clia)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[37m: calling decode_bytes\u001b[26;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.002, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[97mCreateMutex/OpenMutex (zero hits; method validated on a known pair).\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                               \r\n\u001b[97mCross-posted the \u001b[Cecovered RC4\u001b[Ckey/pipelin\u001b[C to #q-\u001b[2Cring-table (!84) and annotated the kill-switch in Ghidra @\r\n0x14002a96d.\u001b[39m                                                                                         \r\n                                                                    \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Himalia)\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97mThe parse function at 0x140025b64 wr\u001b[Ct\u001b[Cs JSON-config flags to context offsets 0x40–0x44. Let me independently verify\r\nthe key names, especially that global DAT_1400b0cf0 (used for offset +0x40 — the flag the orchestrator tests before\r\ncalling self-delete) is\u001b[93m self_delete\u001b[97m:\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                         "]
