[0.004, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[97mscreenshot upload, and\u001b[Clast beacon — but\u001b[1m only if\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m the C2 JSON\u001b[Cc\u001b[Cnfig key\u001b[93m self_delete\u001b[97m (pars\u001b[Cd @ 0x140025b64 into\u001b[39m \r\n\u001b[97mctx+0x40, key global DAT_1400b0cf0, independently re-decoded) is t\u001b[Cue.\u001b[39m                                               \r\n                                      \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[39m                                                                                                                     \r\n\u001b[97m■ Swarm(Io) \u001b[2Cnished: 6 succeeded, 0 failed\u001b[39m                                                                      \u001b[10;1H\u001b[93m💬 reply #q-crypto-keys\u001b[36m\u001b[1m main\u001b(B\u001b[m                 \r\n\u001b[93mAnswered by the string-table and networking analyses:\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                               \r\n\u001b[93m- The on\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93mly embedded key material is the\u001b[1m RC4 key\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m CgeOvEO7hu (10 bytes, literal at 0x14007d6e0, loaded into the global\r\nstd::string at 0x1400b0b30 by init_rc4_keys_and_decrypt_api_names @ 0x140001ee0). It protects the\u001b[1m embedded string table\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m(276 Base64+RC4 entries decoded in #q-string-table, evidence !55/!59/!63/!68\u001b[C: API names for runtime resolution, the C2\r\nendpoint http://45.93.20.28/3d15e67552d448ff.php, build ID 512e7bd984984fb6, exfil filenames, and command strings.\r\n- It does\u001b[1m not\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m protect C2 traffic (traffic is plain base64(JSON) over HTTP, see #q-networking !67), staged payloads, or\r\nvictim files.\u001b[39m                                                                                                 \r\n\u001b[93m- Detector \"candidate AES key\" findings were\u001b[1m disproved\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (!73): they are string-table ciphertexts whose plaintexts are\r\n16/32-char API names.\r\n- 0x140001e10 is\u001b[1m not\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m a crypto ctor — it is the std::bad_array_new_length exception ctor (CRT), per #q-main-flow\r\nanalysis.\u001b[39m                                  \u001b[24;64H           \u001b[C     \u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠼ \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90mThinking…\u001b[39m \u001b[35m\u001b[1mmain\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[37m: calling create\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[26;2H"]
[0.025, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[93mvictim files.\u001b[39m                                                                                                 \r\n\u001b[93m- Detector \"candidate AES key\" findings were\u001b[1m disproved\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (!73): they are string-table ciphertexts whose plaintexts are\r\n16/32-char API names.\r\n- 0x140001e10 is\u001b[1m not\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m a crypto ctor — it is the std::bad_array_new_length exception ctor (CRT), per #q-main-flow\r\nanalysis.\u001b[39m                                  \u001b[10;13H\u001b[93mransomware\u001b[36m\u001b[1m main\u001b(B\u001b[m \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mRansomware refuted.\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m Evidenc\u001b[2Cfrom #q-main-flow, #q-\u001b[Ctring-table, #q-persistence:\u001b[13;7Hcrypto flagged at\u001b[C0x140002b6c\u001b[Cis\u001b[1m inbound string deobfuscation\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (Base64+RC4 with key CgeOvEO7hu)\u001b[Cof the sample's\r\nown embedded strings — not\u001b[Cencryp\u001b[Cion of victim files. 0x140001\u001b[C10 is the CRT std::bad_array_new_length ctor, not\u001b[39m      \r\n\u001b[93mcrypto.\u001b[39m                                                                                                                \r\n\u001b[93m- File enumeration feeds a\u001b[1m file grabber for exfiltration\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (orch\u001b[Cstrator @ 0x140029f68 → grabber @ 0x140008b30, config\r\nsupplied by the C2), not\u001b[Can encryp\u001b[Cion loop.\u001b[CCollected data is POSTed to http://45.93.20.28/3d15e67552d448ff.php in\u001b[C256\r\nK\u001b[CB chunks (upload_file JSON messages, #q-networking !67).\u001b[19;3HAmong the 276 decoded strings there is \u001b[1mno ran\u001b[Com note text, no extension-rename logic, no file-encryption vocabulary\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m.\r\n- The FindNextFile hit at 0x14005c1f7 is dead CRT argv-wildcard code (#q-anti-analysis !75).\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                 