[0.005, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[90m┌─────────────┬────────┬──────────────┬───────────────┐\u001b[39m                                                              \r\n\u001b[90m│\u001b[36m\u001b[1m token       \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90m│\u001b[36m\u001b[1m base64 \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90m│\u001b[36m\u001b[1m plaintext    \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90m│\u001b[36m\u001b[1m slot          \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90m│\u001b[39m                                       \r\n\u001b[90m├─────────────┼────────┼──────────────┼───────────────┤\u001b[39m                 \r\n\u001b[90m│\u001b[97m 0x14007d6ec \u001b[90m│\u001b[97m \u001b[93m+ho=\u001b[97m   \u001b[90m│\u001b[97m \u001b[C\u001b[93m1\u001b[97m (day)     \u001b[90m│\u001b[97m DAT_1400b09f0 \u001b[90m│\u001b[39m                              \r\n\u001b[90m│\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m 0x14007d6f4 \u001b[90m│\u001b[97m \u001b[93m+x8=\u001b[97m   \u001b[90m│\u001b[97m \u001b[93m04\u001b[97m (month)   \u001b[90m│\u001b[97m DAT_1400b0e90 \u001b[90m│\u001b[39m                                                          \r\n\u001b[90m│\u001b[97m 0x14007d6fc \u001b[90m│\u001b[97m \u001b[93m+Rs=\u001b[97m   \u001b[90m│\u001b[97m \u001b[93m20\u001b[97m (year hi) \u001b[90m│\u001b[97m DAT_1400b1ab0 \u001b[90m│\u001b[39m                                                              \r\n\u001b[90m│\u001b[97m 0x14007d704 \u001b[90m│\u001b[97m \u001b[93m+R4=\u001b[97m   \u001b[90m│\u001b[97m \u001b[93m25\u001b[97m (year lo) \u001b[90m│\u001b[97m DAT_1400b1e10 \u001b[90m│\r\n└─────────────┴────────┴──────────────┴───────────────┘\u001b[39m                                                             \r\n                                         \r\n\u001b[93mbuild_expiry_date_string_from_tab\u001b[Ce\u001b[97m @ 0x14002a4c0 streams them as\u001b[93m E1 << '/' <<\u001b[CE2 <<\u001b[C'/' << E3 << E4\u001b[97m (the\u001b[93m '/'\u001b[97m inserter\r\n\u001b[93mFUN_1400306b0\u001b[97m is called exactly twice; byte at 0x1400814a4 =\u001b[93m 2f\u001b[97m), producing\u001b[93m 11/04/2025\u001b[97m.\u001b[39m                            \r\n                                                            \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mComparison semantics\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (\u001b[93mstealc_main_operation\u001b[97m @ 0x14002a774): returns\u001b[93m mktime(expiry) < mktime(now)\u001b[97m — true ⇔ expired\r\n(expiry = 00:00:00 local on 11 Apr 2025, vs.\u001b[93m localtime\u001b[97m of the current clock). In WinMain @ 0x14002a88c:\u001b[93m if (!expired)\r\nstealc_orchestrator_collect_exfil_selfdelete();\u001b[97m —\u001b[1m when the current date is past the expiry, the entire payload\r\n(collection, C2, loader tasks, self-delete) is skipped and WinMain returns 0 for a clean, silent exit\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (no ExitProcess\r\non that path). Failure paths are harder: a\u001b[Cmalformed date\u001b[Cor localtime f\u001b[Cilure →\u001b[93m ExitProcess(0)\u001b[97m. Practical consequence:\r\non any current clock this build detonates as apparently benign; sandbox analysis requires backdating the clock before\r\n11 April 2025.\u001b[39m                                                     \u001b[26;2H"]
