[0.005, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[94m3.\u001b[97m\u001b[1m Decompiler dataflow\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m: the full decompile of 0x14003c2ac shows the identical\u001b[93m DAT_<slot> =\r\n(*pfn_GetProcAddress)(module, &DAT_<name-slot>)\u001b[97m pairings.\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                                    \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mAPI-name identities re-verified independently\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m: script\u001b[93m decode_name_slots\u001b[97m re-derived each name-slot→ciphertext pairing\r\nfrom the raw bytes of\u001b[93m init_string_table_b64_rc4\u001b[97m @ 0x140002b6c (520 LEA events, nearest-preceding-.rdata-literal rule —\r\nnot \u001b[Caken\u001b[Cfrom \u001b[Che \u001b[Corum tabl\u001b[C), read each NUL-terminated base64 token, and decoded it with the native pipeline\u001b[93m [base64\r\n→ RC4 key \"CgeOvEO7hu\"]\u001b[97m. All 13 plaintexts match the expected names byte-for-byte (e.g. token\u001b[93m ml7teWwrsXTa/vxu\u001b[97m @\r\n0x14007e290 →\u001b[93m QueueUserAPC\u001b[97m).\u001b[39m                                             \u001b[13;1H\u001b[97m\u001b[1mCall-through pointer identity\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m: all 100 GetProcAddress-style calls (incl. all 13 above) go through slot\u001b[1m 0x1400b4df8 =\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93mpfn_GetProcAddress\u001b[97m, wri\u001b[Cten once @ 0x14003c117 in\u001b[93m resolve_dynamic_apis_core_kernel32_advapi32\u001b[C\u001b[97mas\u001b[39m                 \r\n\u001b[93mGetProcAddress(hmod_kernel32, DAT_1400b0db0 /* decrypts to \"GetProcAddress\" */)\u001b[97m; the 10 calls through 0x1400b4df0 are\r\nthe\u001b[93m pfn_LoadLibraryA\u001b[97m module loads (written @ 0x14003c13e).\u001b[18;1HThis confirms with verified identities the full early-bird QueueUserAPC injection API set (CreateProcessA →\r\nVirtualAllocEx → WriteProcessMemory → QueueUserAPC → ResumeThread → WaitForSingleObject → VirtualFreeEx) plus the\r\nnamed-pipe comms set (CreateNamedPipeA, ReadFile, ConvertStringS