[0.007, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[93m📌 #q-tls-callbacks — Does the TLS directory at RVA 0x82C00 register any TLS callbacks?\u001b[36m\u001b[1m main\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93mTriage (#q-triage !57) found a TLS directory at RVA 0x82C00 (VA 0x140082c00) but it was never inspected. Read the\r\nIMAGE_TLS_DIRECTORY64 fields and the AddressOfCallBacks array: are there any TLS callbacks that run before the entry\r\npoint (a common anti-debug/early-init trick), or is this just CRT boilerplate (empty/null callback list)? Give the raw\r\nbytes and, if c\u001b[Cllbacks \u001b[Cxist,\u001b[Canalyze each c\u001b[Cllback function.\u001b[39m                              \r\n                                                                                                                 \r\n\u001b[90m○\u001b[39m \u001b[90mmain · ▸ reverse_engineer(Complete static analysis of a Stealc v2…) · …running\u001b[39m                                    \r\n                                                                                                                      \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Megaclite)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                 \r\n\u001b[97m▶ ReverseEngineer(Megaclite) — goal: Complete static analysis of a Stealc v2 infostealer sample; close the last\r\nanti-analysis gap.\u001b[39m                                                              \u001b[16;1H\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Megaclite) · ▸ read(0x140082c00) · 96 chars\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                               \r\n\u001b[31m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Megaclite) · ▸ read_file(0x81E00) · 96 chars\u001b[20;1H\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Megaclite)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                \r\n\u001b[97mRaw read failed on hex string; re-reading with decimal offset, and resolving the AddressOfCallBacks array at\r\n0x14006fc68 (parsed from the directory):\u001b[39m                      \u001b[26;2H"]
