[0.008, "o", "\u001b[4;1H \u001b[C                                                              \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Megaclite)\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97mOff-by-one in my decimal conversion — correct file offset for RVA 0x6FC68 is 0x6EE68 = 454248:\u001b[8;1H\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Megaclite) · ▸ read_file(454248) · 3 lines\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                              \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Megaclite)\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97mCallback array confirmed empty by two independent routes (Ghidra memory read + raw file bytes). One last check —\r\nidentify the two pointers that follow the null terminators, to show they belong to a different CRT table and are not\r\ncallbacks:\u001b[39m                   \r\n                                                                                                                \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mRevers\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90meEngineer(Megaclite) · ▸ get_function(0x1400538b4) · 409 chars\u001b[39m                                              \r\n          \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Megaclite) · ▸ get_function(0x140065804) · 256 chars\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                                    \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Megaclite) · ▸ read(0x140084e38) · 16 chars\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                                    \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Megaclite)\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97mAll evidence is in. Posting the answer under #q-tls-callbacks:\u001b[26;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.004, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[93m0006ee78  b4 38 05 40 01 00 00 00  04 58 06 40 01 00 00 00   <- next, unrelated table\r\n```\u001b[39m                          \r\n                                                                                              \r\n\u001b[93mThe very first entry is NULL. The Windows loader (and the CRT's __dyn_tls_init) walk this array until the first NULL\r\npointer, so\u001b[1m zero callbacks are registered\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m. The two NULL qwords are the linker's .CRT$XLA/.CRT$XLZ sentinels with\r\nnothing emitted between them — exactly what MSVC produces when the program declares no __declspec(thread) callbacks and\r\nno manual _tls_used entries.\u001b[39m \r\n                                                                                                                \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1m3. The pointers after the terminator are NOT callbacks\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m: 0x1400538b4 is FID-identified CRT __acrt_uninitialize_locale\r\n(\"Library Function - Single Match\", VS2017/2019 Release) and 0x140065804 \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93mis a 28-byte stub in the same CRT region —\r\nthese belong to the adjacent CRT uninitializer pointer table that merely follows the TLS sentinels in .rdata; they sit\r\n\u001b[1mafter\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m the NULL terminator and are never reached by the TLS-callback walk. xrefs_to 0x14006fc68 shows no code references\r\neither (only the loader/TLS directory consume it).\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                                    \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mConclusion:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m the TLS directory exists only because the statically-linked MSVC 14.43 CRT always emits _tls_used (8-byte\r\nTLS template, _tls_index, aligned-4 characteristics). There is\u001b[1m no TLS-callback anti-debug or early-init code\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m; this\r\ncloses the last anti-analysis gap consistently with #q-anti-analysis (!83/!88): the sample's only genuine anti-analysis\r\nis the CIS locale gate, the named-event single-instance gate, the build-expiry kill-switch, and the\r\nstring-encryption/runtime-API-resolution obfuscation layer.\u001b[39m   \u001b[24;59H\u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠏ \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90mThinking…\u001b[39m \u001b[35m\u001b[1mReverseEngine\u001b[2C(Megaclite)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[37m: calling cre\u001b[Cte_comm\u001b[Cnt\u001b[26;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
