[0.007, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[97mAll tokens verified by independent native decode. One last byte-level check of the bootstrap write at 0x14003c117:\u001b[6;1H\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mDeveloper(Taygete) · ▸ run_script(rip_scan) · 460 chars\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                  \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Developer(Taygete)\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97mEverything is verified. The bootstrap sequence is: static-import\u001b[93m GetProcAddress\u001b[97m call at 0x14003c0f3 (name = decoded\r\nslot 0x1400b0db0 \"GetProcAddress\") → result stored to 0x1400b4df8 at 0x14003c117, then\u001b[93m call rax\u001b[97m resolves LoadLibraryA.\r\nLet me persist annotations in the project and post the findings:\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                   \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mDeveloper(Taygete) · ▸ rename_symbol(DAT_1400b4de0) · 159 chars\u001b[39m                                                     \r\n                                                                \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mDeveloper(Taygete) · ▸ rename_symbol(DAT_1400b4dd0) · 115 chars\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                               \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mDeveloper(Taygete) · ▸ set_comment(14003c62d) · 97 chars\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                               \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mDeveloper(Taygete) · ▸ set_comment(14003cce9) · 97 chars\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                        \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Developer(Taygete)\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97mNow posting the findings as evidence under #q-string-table:\u001b[26;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.004, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[93mdescriptor for the ABE-key named pipe, which is exactly this API's job. Slot renamed\u001b[39m                              \r\n\u001b[93mpfn_ConvertStringSecurityDescriptorToSecurityDescriptorA.\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                       \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1m4. Code site 0x14003cce9 → resolves\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m ReadFile\u001b[1m (kernel32).\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m call qword [0x1400b4df8] with RCX = [0x1400b4cd8] (kernel32\r\nhandle, written @ 0x14003c0c9 by the core resolver's LoadLibraryA(\"kernel32.dll\")) and RDX = c_str of decoded slot\r\n\u001b[1m0x1400b1790\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (lea @ 0x14003cccc / cmova @ 0x14003ccda; token @ 0x14007df50 mU7paE8XrnQ= → re-decoded natively to\u001b[39m    \r\n\u001b[93mReadFile).\u001b[39m                                                                                                            \r\n                                                                \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1m5. Code site 0x14003cd0c →\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m MOV [0x1400b4dd0], RAX\u001b[1m = stores the R\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[93m\u001b[1meadFile pointer.\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m Same pipelined pattern: RAX = result\r\nof the call @ 0x14003cce9; the intervening LEA/CMOVA load the\u001b[3m next\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m name (0x1400b1fd0 = GetFileSizeEx, call @\r\n0x14003cd13, stored @ 0x14003cd36 → 0x1400b4dc0). Consumer check: 0x1400b4dd0 is read by\r\nread_entire_file_to_localalloc_buffer @ 0x14001a905, collect_browser_profile_and_get_abe_key_via_pipe @ 0x14001f5a0,\r\nchrome_localstate_dpapi_decrypt_v10_masterkey_and_exfil @ 0x14001aafc, and FUN_14003a874 @ 0x14003a97c — all file-read\r\ncall sites, consistent with ReadFile. Slot renamed pfn_ReadFile.\u001b[19;1HNeighboring stanzas decoded in the same pass (context, byte-verified): call @ 0x14003c603 → RegCloseKey (0x1400b1550)\r\nstored @ 0x14003c626 → 0x1400b4e40; call @ 0x14003c657 → RegOpenKeyExA stored @ 0x14003c65d → 0x1400b4e50; store @\r\n0x14003cce2 → 0x1400b4d40 = CreateFileW (0x1400b2030, call @ 0x14003ccbf); call @ 0x14003cd3d → CreateNamedPipeA\r\n(0x1400b03b0). EOL comments persisted in \u001b(B\u001b[m"]
