[0.011, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[90m│\u001b[97m \u001b[1m0x14003c650\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (store)       \u001b[90m│\u001b[97m → slot \u001b[1m0x1400b4de0\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m                         \u001b[90m│\u001b[97m Pipelined \u001b[93mMOV [slot],RAX\u001b[97m saving the result \u001b[90m│\r\n│\u001b[97m                           \u001b[90m│\u001b[97m                                            \u001b[90m│\u001b[97m of the call @ 0x14003c62d; sole consumer   \u001b[90m│\r\n│\u001b[97m                           \u001b[90m│\u001b[97m                                            \u001b[90m│\u001b[97m is the ABE named-pipe security-descriptor  \u001b[90m│\r\n│\u001b[97m                           \u001b[90m│\u001b[97m                                            \u001b[90m│\u001b[97m code @ 0x14001f3ee                         \u001b[90m│\r\n│\u001b[97m \u001b[1m0x14003cce9\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (call)        \u001b[90m│\u001b[97m \u001b[93mReadFile\u001b[97m             \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m                      \u001b[90m│\u001b[97m \u001b[93m(*pfn_GetProcAddress)(kernel32, name)\u001b[97m —    \u001b[90m│\r\n│\u001b[97m                           \u001b[90m│\u001b[97m                                            \u001b[90m│\u001b[97m name from decoded slot 0x1400b1790 (token  \u001b[90m│\r\n│\u001b[97m                           \u001b[90m│\u001b[97m                                            \u001b[90m│\u001b[97m @ 0x14007df50 \u001b[93mmU7paE8XrnQ=\u001b[97m)                \u001b[90m│\r\n│\u001b[97m \u001b[1m0x14003cd0c\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (store)       \u001b[90m│\u001b[97m → slot \u001b[1m0x1400b4dd0\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m                         \u001b[90m│\u001b[97m Pipelined store of the ReadFile pointer;   \u001b[90m│\r\n│\u001b[97m                           \u001b[90m│\u001b[97m                                            \u001b[90m│\u001b[97m consumed by 4 file-reading routines (incl. \u001b[90m│\r\n│\u001b[97m                           \u001b[90m│\u001b[97m                                            \u001b[90m│\u001b[97m \u001b[93mread_entire_file_to_localalloc_buffer\u001b[97m,     \u001b[90m│\r\n│\u001b[97m                           \u001b[90m│\u001b[97m                                            \u001b[90m│\u001b[97m Chrome Local State decryptor)              \u001b[90m│\r\n└───────────────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────┘\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                      \r\n\u001b[97mVerification was done by two independent routes: (1) raw-byte RIP-relative stanza decoding (\u001b[93mrip_scan\u001b[97m session script,\r\nbypassing the 100-instruction disassembly cap), and (2) native\u001b[93m decode_bytes [base64 → RC4(\"CgeOvEO7hu\")]\u001b[97m re-decode of\r\neach name token (\u001b[93mverify_tokens\u001b[97m). The slot→name pairings explicitly applied the\u001b[39m                                       \r\n\u001b[93mpitfall-pipelined-getprocaddress-slot-stores\u001b[97m rule — each store saves the\u001b[3m previous\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m call's result — and each slot was\r\ncross-checked against its consumer-side xrefs. I also persisted the findings in the Ghidra project (renamed both slots\r\nto\u001b[93m pfn_ConvertStringSecurityD\u001b[CscriptorToSecurityDescriptorA\u001b[97m /\u001b[93m pfn_ReadFile\u001b[97m and left EOL comments at both call sites).\u001b[26;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
