[0.007, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[93m- xref_check — 10-line WRITE-xref lister per slot. Trivial one-off; native xrefs_to wrapper. \u001b[1mSkip.\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[C                                                                       \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mNot readable before cutoff (tool access revoked):\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[C                    \r\n\u001b[93m- disasm_window, slot_map_dataflow — session copies SHADOWING existing library scripts of the same names. Unless they\r\ncontain fixes (unverified), no overwrite-promotion is justified.\r\n- grep_decomp — likely duplicate of library decomp_grep; rip_scan — likely overlaps library\r\nresolve_globals/blob_to_global/rip_disp_range_scan (all proven on this very sample per their docs); decode_name_slots —\r\nlikely covered by library dynapi_resolver_join/slot_map_dataflow; check_disasm_len, probe_disasm — names indicate\r\none-off environment probes.\u001b[39m                                                                                        \r\n                                                             \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mDecision: nothing promoted.\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m Rationale: the two read-and-generic candidates are either redundant with stronger library\r\nscripts proven on this same family (verify_tokens, decode_string_table) or trivial (xref_check); the rest could not be\r\nverified before the context limit, and unverified scripts must not be promoted.\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                          \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mRemaining work for a future curator:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m read rip_scan, decode_name_slots, grep_decomp and the two shadows (disasm_window,\r\nslot_map_dataflow); diff shadows against the library versions and overwrite-promote only if they fix something;\r\noptionally promote decode_string_table as b64rc4_xref_pair_decode with an honest \"4th cross-check route, xref-order\r\ncaveat\" description.\u001b[39m                                                               \u001b[24;110H\u001b[37mcreate_pos\u001b[26;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
