[0.007, "o", "\u001b[4;1H                                                                                                  \r\n\u001b[97m- Listed all 10 session scripts and the full library.\r\n- Read 3 session sources before tool access was cut:\r\n-\u001b[93m decode_string_table\u001b[97m (xref-pairing base64+RC4 decoder) — fully args-parameterized and generic, but redundant with\r\nthree stronger library routes already proven on Stealc v2 (\u001b[93mharvest\u001b[97m,\u001b[93m rc4_b64_strings\u001b[97m,\u001b[39m                                 \r\n\u001b[93mra\u001b[Cge_b64rc4\u001b[97m/\u001b[93mrdata_b64_native_scan\u001b[97m), and its xref-order pairing heuristic is fragile. Only marginal promotion value.\r\n-\u001b[C\u001b[93mverify_t\u001b[Ckens\u001b[97m — superseded by library\u001b[93m verify_blobs\u001b[97m /\u001b[93m token\u001b[Cpipeline_d\u001b[Ccode\u001b[97m (which add NUL-truncation safety and\r\narbitrary pipelines). Skipped.\u001b[39m                                                                                         \r\n\u001b[97m    - \u001b[93mxref_check\u001b[97m — trivial 10-line \u001b[93mxrefs_to\u001b[97m WRITE filter, one-off. Skipped.\u001b[39m                                      \r\n                           \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mWhy nothing was promoted:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m the only read-and-generic candidates are redundant or trivial, and the remaining 7 scripts\r\n(\u001b[93mdisasm_window\u001b[97m and\u001b[93m slot_map_d\u001b[2Caflow\u001b[97m — which shadow existing library scripts — plus\u001b[93m \u001b[Cip_scan\u001b[97m,\u001b[93m decode_name_slots\u001b[97m,\u001b[39m     \r\n\u001b[93mgrep_decomp\u001b[97m,\u001b[93m check_d\u001b[2Ca\u001b[Cm_len\u001b[97m,\u001b[93m probe_disasm\u001b[97m) could not be read/verified before the context ceiling; promoting\u001b[39m         \r\n\u001b[97munverified or unread scripts would violate the library-quality rules.\u001b[39m          \u001b[19;1H\u001b[97m\u001b[1mWhat remains (documented in the forum post):\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m a future curator should read the 7 unread scripts, diff the two shadows\u001b[39m  \r\n\u001b[97magainst their library versions (overwrite-promote only if they contain fixes), and optionally promote\u001b[39m          \r\n\u001b[93mdecode_string_table\u001b[97m as a low-priority cross-check tool (suggested name\u001b[C\u001b[93mb64rc4_xref_pair_decode\u001b[97m) with the xref-order\r\ncaveat stated honestly.\u001b[26;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
