[0.008, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[97m(\u001b[93mdisasm_window\u001b[97m and\u001b[93m slot_map_dataflow\u001b[97m — which shadow existing library scripts — plus\u001b[93m rip_scan\u001b[97m,\u001b[93m decode_name_slots\u001b[97m,\r\n\u001b[93mgrep_decomp\u001b[97m,\u001b[93m check_disasm_len\u001b[97m,\u001b[93m probe_disasm\u001b[97m) could not be read/verified before the context ceiling; promoting\r\nunverified or unread scrip\u001b[Cs w\u001b[Cu\u001b[Cd\u001b[Cviolate th\u001b[C library-quality\u001b[Crules.\u001b[39m                                               \r\n                                                                                                                \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mWhat remains (documented in the forum post):\u001b[C\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97ma future curator should read the 7 unread scripts, diff the \u001b[Cwo shadows\r\nagainst thei\u001b[2Clibr\u001b[Cry versions (overwrite-promote onl\u001b[C if the\u001b[2Ccontain fixes), and optionally promote\r\n\u001b[93mde\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93mcode_string_table\u001b[97m as a low-priority cross-check tool (suggested name\u001b[93m b64rc4_xref_pair_decode\u001b[97m) with the xref-order\r\ncaveat stated honestly.\u001b[39m                                                                                             \r\n                                                                                                     \r\n\u001b[31m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mmain · ▸ finish() · 362 chars\u001b[39m                                                                                    \r\n                       \r\n\u001b[90m○\u001b[Cmain · ▸ researcher(Persist durable generic lessons from th…) · …running\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                             \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Researcher(Harpalyke)\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m▶ Researcher(Harpalyke) — goal: Persist durable generic lessons from the Stealc v2 static-analysis run into the\r\ncross-run memory library.\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b