[0.057, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Researcher(Harpalyke)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                                           \r\n\u001b[97m▶ R\u001b[Csearcher(Harpalyke) — goal: Persist durable generic lessons from the Stealc v2 static-analysis run into the\r\ncross-run memory library.\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                             \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Researcher(Harpalyke)\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97mI'll review the run's lessons against existing memories. First, let me check what's already saved.\u001b[11;1H\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mResearcher(Harpalyke) · ▸ read_memory(family-intel-stealc-v1-v2) · 43 lines\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                               \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mResearcher(Harpalyke) · ▸ search_memories(TLS callback) · 2 chars\u001b[15;1H\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mResearcher(Harpalyke) · ▸ search_memories(deterministic ciphertext) · 2 chars\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                  \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Researcher(Harpalyke)\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97mThe family memory already covers candidate 1 (expiry kill-switch, including the 4-entry\u001b[93m %d/%m/%Y\u001b[97m assembly, silent clean\r\nexit, and clock-backdating advice — amended earlier per !80/!111) and candidates 3/4 exist as pitfalls. Candidate 2's\r\ndetails (exact verb set\u001b[93m create/loader/upload_file/done\u001b[97m, task-type ints, drop paths) are NOT fully in the family memory\r\n— it still records an older\u001b[93m loginr\u001b[97m verb and lacks the loader-task specifics, so I'll amend it. Candidates 5 and 6 have\r\nno existing memory (searches returned nothing) — I'll save them as new techniques.\u001b[24;63H\u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠹\u001b[34;57H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90m2\u001b[10C9\u001b[C5\u001b[C6\u001b[C0\u001b[10C9\u001b[C694\u001b[13C32\u001b[2C364\u001b[8C64\u001b[26;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.004, "o", "\u001b[5;1H\u001b[97mI'll review the run's lessons again\u001b[Ct existing memories. First,\u001b[Clet me check what's already saved.\u001b[39m             \r\n                         \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mResearcher(Harpalyke) · ▸ read_memory(family-intel-stealc-v1-v2) · 43 lines\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                      \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mResearcher(Harpalyke) · ▸ search_memories(TLS callback) · 2 chars\u001b[39m                               \u001b[11;29H\u001b[90ms\u001b[2Crch_\u001b[Cemories(determini\u001b[2Cic \u001b[Ciphertext) ·\u001b[C2 chars\u001b[13;1H\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Researcher(Harpalyke)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                           \r\n\u001b[97mThe family memory already covers candidate 1 (expiry kill-switch, including the 4-entry\u001b[93m %d/%m/%Y\u001b[97m assembly, silent clean\r\nexit, and clock-backdating advice — amended earlier per !80/!111) and candidates 3/4 exist as pitfalls. Candidate 2's\r\ndeta\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97mils (exact verb set\u001b[93m create/loader/upload_file/done\u001b[97m, task-type ints, drop paths) are NOT fully in the family memory\r\n— it still records an older\u001b[93m loginr\u001b[97m verb and lacks the loader-task specifics, so I'll amend it. Candidates 5 and 6 have\r\nno existing memory (s\u001b[2Crches returne\u001b[C no\u001b[Ching) — I'll save them as \u001b[Cew techniques.\u001b[39m                                     \r\n                                                                                                                     \r\n\u001b[31m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mResearcher(Harpalyke) · ▸ save_memory(technique-prove-string-absence-fixed-rc…) · 41 chars\u001b[39m                          \r\n                                                                                                                      \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mResearcher(Harpalyke) · ▸ save_memory(technique-verify-empty-tls-callback-arr…) · 159 chars\u001b[24;63H\u001b[39m    \u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠹ \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90mThinking…\u001b[39m \u001b[35m\u001b[1mResea\u001b[Cche\u001b[C(Harpalyke)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[37m: calling save_\u001b[Cemory\u001b[26;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
