[0.009, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[97mexit, and clock-backdating advice — amended earlier per !80/!111) and candidates 3/4 exist as pitfalls. Candidate 2's\r\ndetails (exact verb set\u001b[93m create/loader/upload_file/done\u001b[97m, task-type ints, drop paths) are NOT fully in the family memory\r\n— it still records an older\u001b[93m loginr\u001b[97m verb and lacks the loader-task specifics, so I'll amend it. Candidates 5 and 6 have\r\nno existing memory (searches returned nothing) — I'll save them as new techniques.\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                      \r\n\u001b[31m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mResearcher(Harpalyke) · ▸ save_memory(technique-prove-string-absence-fixed-rc…) · 41 chars\u001b[39m                           \r\n                                                                                                                     \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mResearcher(Harpalyke) · ▸ save_memory(technique-verify-empty-tls-callback-arr…) · 159 chars\u001b[39m                         \r\n                                                                                                                      \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Researcher(Harpalyke)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                          \r\n\u001b[97mThe TLS memory saved; the first name was too long. Retrying with a shorter name:\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                                                          \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mResearcher(Harpalyke) · ▸ save_memory(technique-prove-absence-fixed-rc4-keyst…) · 158 chars\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                                                           \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Researcher(Harpalyke)\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97mNow amending\u001b[93m family-intel-stealc-v1-v2\u001b[97m with the verified C2 verb vocabulary and loader-task specifics (it currently\r\nrecords\u001b[Can \u001b[Clder/unverified\u001b[93m loginr\u001b[97m verb and lacks task-type\u001b[Cin\u001b[Cs, drop paths, and chunk sizes):\u001b[22;1H\u001b[90m○\u001b[39Cfamily-intel-ste\u001b[Clc-v1-v2) · …\u001b[Cunning\u001b[39m                \u001b[26;2H"]
