[0.022, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[93mrecorded loginr so verb spellings are per-build detail; both uploader chunk sizes (file-based 0x40000 = 256 KiB,\r\nbuffer-based 0x7D000 = 512,000 bytes, the latter base64ing filename too); loader task-type ints 0=EXE /\r\n1=PowerShell-IEX (fileless, hardcoded SysWOW64 powershell path) / 2=msiexec /passive, drop path <CSIDL 0–6 dir>\\<rand12\r\nmt19937>.exe|.msi with the full csidl→CSIDL mapping, SW_HIDE, 10× retry (!98–!101); and the dead-flag observation\r\n(take_screenshot/steal_outlook parsed-but-unread, screenshot unconditional, !105).\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mSkipped as duplicates (already in the library):\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[C                                                                                           \r\n\u001b[94m1.\u001b[93m Build-expiry kill-switch pattern — already fully covered by the [PER-BUILD] section of family-intel-stealc-v1-v2\r\n(ame\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[93mnded earlier this run per !80: 4-entry %d/%m/%Y assembly, silent clean exit, backdate-the-clock note, 3-step check\r\nrecipe, and the caut\u001b[Con about one run mis-recording \"absent\").\u001b[39m                                                     \r\n\u001b[94m2.\u001b[93m MSVC store-pipelining in\u001b[CGetProcAddress resolvers — exists as pitfall-pipelined-getprocaddress-slot-stores\r\n(re-validated this run in !107/!113; body already states the dataflow-not-adjacency rule, no change needed).\r\n\u001b[94m3.\u001b[93m \"AES keys\" that are really encrypted string-table entries / T1486 flags on string-table init — covered by\r\npitfall-carved-b64-keys-are-encrypted-strings + pitfall-t1486-flags-from-c2-rc4-and-sandbox-dir-counting (confirmed\r\napplicable in !73/!65).\u001b[39m                                                       \u001b[21;1H\u001b[93mAlso noted: family-intel-stealc-v2-chrome-abe-srdi-internals was already saved mid-run (!111) — no further changes\r\nneeded\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[93m there.\u001b[39m                                                    "]
